course: dictionary
lesson: 2281
title: A place of goodbye
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words are about things that are sad or hard to talk about. Adults sometimes use a gentle phrase instead of a plain one, and you need to know both to understand what people mean. A crematorium is a building where the body of a person who has died is turned to ashes by great heat.
explain: Context clues help you here. «At many crematorium services curtains close around the coffin at the end, as a sign of goodbye.» The words service, coffin and goodbye tell you that a crematorium is a place where families say goodbye to someone who has died.
explain: Adults may say «Going to the crematorium» instead of a plainer phrase. This is a euphemism, a gentle way of saying something hard. Crematorium is a noun, and its plural can be crematoriums or crematoria. When you are unsure, ask an adult you trust, or check a dictionary.
fact: A crematorium is a building where the body of a person who has died is turned to ashes.
fact: «Cremation» means the process of turning a body to ashes by great heat at a crematorium.
fact: «Coffin» means the long box that holds the body of a person who has died.
fact: Often there is a funeral service in a small chapel at the crematorium first.
fact: A euphemism is a gentle word or phrase used instead of a harder one, such as «going to the crematorium» instead of a plainer phrase.
exercise: «At many crematorium services curtains close around the coffin at the end, as a sign of goodbye.» What is a crematorium? | A school hall where children sing | *A building where a body is turned to ashes, often with a service first | A shop that sells flowers and cards | A park with a pond and swings
exercise: Find and copy one word from this sentence that means the long box that holds the body. «The coffin is the long box that holds the body of the person who died.» | person | *coffin | body | box
exercise: Adults say «Going to the crematorium» instead of a plainer phrase. What is this kind of gentle phrase called? | A synonym for sad | A compound word | *A euphemism | A proverb
test: «Cremation means the body is turned to ashes by great heat at a crematorium.» What does cremation mean? | *The process of turning a body to ashes by great heat | A long box for the body | A grave dug in the ground | A party for a birthday
test: Which is one of the two correct plurals of crematorium? | crematorial | crematorias | *crematoria | crematorium's
exam: «They held a service at the crematorium.» What does this tell the reader? | A family is having a picnic in the park | The children are going on a trip | *Someone has died and the family is saying goodbye | A new building is being built
